{# The date shortcuts of the agenda, the first way through it ("what's on tonight?"), each with its count of the page's
   other filters (EventElasticaRepository::getFacets()). "Tous les jours" leaves the period out of the URL. Not followed,
   their dates changing every day, but for the date pages of a busy location ("/toulouse/ce-week-end"): those are meant
   to be found (DatePageIndexingPolicy). Above the events, a phone shows them on one line scrolled sideways (they took
   three lines before the first event); the filters panel wraps them, all in sight.

   Twice on a page: above the events, headed on a phone by the button of the filters ({withFilters: true}, the id the
   tests and the links read), and in the phone's filters panel ({withFilters: false}). #}
{% set withFilters = withFilters ?? true %}
<div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2{{ withFilters ? ' chips-scroll-mobile' }}"{% if withFilters %} id="agenda-dates"{% endif %} role="group" aria-label="Dates">
    {% if withFilters %}
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-pill d-lg-none" data-bs-toggle="offcanvas" data-bs-target="#agenda-filters" aria-controls="agenda-filters">
            <twig:Icon name="lucide:sliders-horizontal" />
            Filtres
        </button>
    {% endif %}
    {% for preset in enum_cases('App\\Enum\\DateRangePreset') %}
        {% set count = facets.dates[preset.value] ?? null %}
        {% set when = preset.value == 'anytime' ? {} : {when: preset.value} %}
        {% set followed = datePagesIndexable and preset.pageSlug and not type and not place and not tagEntity and not undatedFilters %}
        <twig:Chip href="{{ agenda_path(location.slug, type: type, place: place, tag: tagEntity, filters: undatedFilters|merge(when)) }}" active="{{ search.preset is same as(preset) }}" class="btn-sm text-nowrap" rel="{{ followed ? false : 'nofollow' }}">
            {{ preset.label }}
            {% if count is not null %}<span class="chip-count">{{ count }}</span>{% endif %}
        </twig:Chip>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
